<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A school fundraiser raised Ksh <m>{6000}</m>. It is shared among the Science, Drama and Music clubs in a ratio <m>a : b : c</m> that you choose. Choose whole numbers so that the Science club gets exactly Ksh <m>{1500}</m>, and the Drama and Music clubs get different amounts. Many answers are correct.</p><p><m>a =</m> <fillin characters="4" name="ansA"/> </p><p><m>b =</m> <fillin characters="4" name="ansB"/> </p><p><m>c =</m> <fillin characters="4" name="ansC"/> </p><p/></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The Science club gets <m>\dfrac{{1500}}{{6000}} = {\frac{1}{4}}</m> of the money, so its share of the parts must be <m>\dfrac{a}{a + b + c} = {\frac{1}{4}}</m>.</p><p>Take <m>a = {1}</m> and <m>a + b + c = {4}</m>, so <m>b + c = {3}</m>. Split <m>{3}</m> into two different whole numbers.</p><p>For example <m>a : b : c = {1} : {1} : {2}</m>. Check: <m>{6000} \times \dfrac{ {1} }{ {4} } = {1500}</m>.</p><p>Any <m>a : b : c</m> with <m>\dfrac{a}{a + b + c} = {\frac{1}{4}}</m> and <m>b \ne c</m> is correct.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>1</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>1</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>2</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>